## Goal
One released batch can be found, claimed, executed, returned and reviewed on this
page, preserving its instructions, Director replies, evidence and unresolved work.
This first use is manual coordination, not an implemented Clerk dispatcher.

## Batch
05.01.md is the first batch: capture the learning and establish the work-book route.
State: packed for Director release. Intended executor: Grok Builder; actual model,
session and claim must be recorded on execution. Merely reading this page is not
permission to run its batch.

## Record locations
- Instructions, release, claim, per-#NN execution results and return: 05.01.md.
- Prime's review of that exact returned revision: review section on 05.01.md.
- Local understanding and findings: 06.01.md, with integration dispositions.
- Reproducible test/check evidence: evidence/ on this page, with a manifest.
- Pinned input identities: source-manifest.tsv.

05.01.md is a working batch. It is not the final consolidated 05 for reusable
execution. Final instructions are compiled only after the method has been exercised
and reviewed. A future batch uses 05.02.md; do not silently replace this record.

## Legacy record
Root packs/ and returns/ remain historical/bootstrap intake. Preserve their bytes
and links. New work for this line lands here, with one authoritative batch/return,
instead of two independently edited copies in the root folders and book.

## Readiness
Established desk accepted by Prime; runtime not active; routing and automatic
wakeup not integrated. A Director-approved release plus explicit file handoff is
the current working mechanism. Model execution within a released scope is useful
before autonomous scheduling is ready.
